\meta{commit}{45563d9}
\import{base-macros}

\p{From the first unit of a completely loaded file that file order cannot decide, the environment pass admits every unit itself, dependencies first. Cycles are unknown constants, as in the official checker, and a unit that depends on a failed one inherits its outcome. Where the official verdict depends on the order of independent declarations (the quotient constants, the headers of mutual blocks, unsafe member records), a simulation of the official replay order on names decides; it was verified against the official checker 4.36.0 on 96 name-only variants and 3,691 tests and mutants. Two follow-ups the same morning restrict both to sessions that cover the whole, completely loaded file, after the driver's invariance suite found that a pipelined run could reject a reordered export that a batch run accepts. Published with 86 tests; the gate is 230 of 230 with 0 soundness and 0 completeness differences on the tutorial and bugs mutants.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-admit/README.md}. Commit \commit{45563d9}. Session: [foundation modules and the reference pipeline](ses-BQZM). Related: [inductive admission](design-inductive-admission).}
